koronus-sector-risk-stable-detail = Brief turbulence or vertigo is possible. Green routes do not cause breaches.
koronus-sector-risk-dangerous-detail = Possible vertigo, psychic storms, a 15-second equipment blackout or a rift aboard. Prepare flashlights and medical supplies.
koronus-sector-risk-unstable-detail = Frequent disturbances and dangerous breaches: a pack, a hunter or corrosive daemons. A rift takes 4 seconds to seal before enemies emerge. Prepare the crew or wait for a safer window.
koronus-sector-map-legend-unstable = UNSTABLE ROUTE
koronus-warp-incident-turbulence = Warp turbulence! The Gellar field holds; remain at your stations.
koronus-warp-incident-rift = Rift aboard! Find the purple anomaly and hold an empty hand on its stabilizer for 4 seconds. Breach in 12 seconds.
koronus-warp-incident-boarders = Gellar field breach! Daemon incursion in 12 seconds. Find and seal the rift or prepare to fight.
koronus-warp-breach = Warp creatures have emerged! Protect the crew.
koronus-warp-sealed = Rift sealed. No more creatures can pass through it.
ent-KoronusWarpRift = unstable warp rift
    .desc = A breach in the Gellar field. Hold an empty hand against its stabilizer to seal it before anything emerges.

koronus-warp-incident-vertigo = Warp vertigo! Your balance will recover in 10 seconds. Stay clear of open airlocks.
koronus-warp-incident-blackout = Electrical front! Equipment is offline for 15 seconds. Find the yellow emergency relay and work with an empty hand for 4 seconds to restore power early. Batteries retain their charge.
koronus-warp-incident-psychicstorm = Psychic storm! Vertigo and slowed movement for 18 seconds. Stay together while the Gellar field suppresses the echo.
koronus-warp-incident-hunt = A greater warp hunter is approaching! Breach in 12 seconds. Seal the rift or fight together.
koronus-warp-incident-corrosivebreach = Corrosive warp creatures are piercing the field! Breach in 12 seconds. Seal the rift or prepare protection and burn treatment.
koronus-warp-salvage = The rift has subsided. An anomalous specimen crate remains on the deck; recover it for research or recycling.
koronus-sector-challenge-extract = Search the ruin, evade or defeat its guards and carry the find outside the location. A survivor must be carried.
koronus-sector-challenge-contain = Defeat the enemies or work at the node with an empty hand for { $seconds } seconds. Movement and damage interrupt containment.
koronus-sector-challenge-work = Work at the objective with an empty hand for { $seconds } seconds. Movement and damage interrupt the work; arrange cover.
koronus-sector-salvage-manifest = Successful expedition cargo: { $manifest }. Collect the crate and bring it aboard.
koronus-salvage-engineering = steel, cable and a high-capacity battery
koronus-salvage-medical = dressings, ointment and ephedrine
koronus-salvage-minerals = gold, silver and plasma ore samples
koronus-salvage-archeotech = an ancient processor, storage drive and encrypted data
koronus-salvage-xenology = anomalous specimens, plasma and research data
ent-KoronusSalvageEngineering = recovered engineering supplies
    .desc = Steel, cable and a battery recovered during an expedition. Bring the cargo aboard.
ent-KoronusSalvageMedical = recovered medical supplies
    .desc = Field supplies for treating the crew after an expedition.
ent-KoronusSalvageMinerals = recovered mineral samples
    .desc = Ore recovered from an explored site. Suitable for processing.
ent-KoronusSalvageArcheotech = recovered archeotech
    .desc = Ancient components and data recovered from an explored site.
ent-KoronusSalvageXenology = recovered anomalous specimens
    .desc = Specimens and data for research. The crate offers no automatic payout.
koronus-warp-power-restored = Emergency relay restored. Power is returning; a recovered repair kit is in a crate on the deck.
ent-KoronusWarpFieldRelay = emergency Gellar field relay
    .desc = An overloaded bypass circuit. Work on it with an empty hand for 4 seconds to restore power early.
